  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tr&#xf3;caire Human Rights Consortia 2022 -2025</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Tr&#xf3;caire Human Rights Consortia 2022-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d genom Tr&#xf3;caire till ett MR-konsortium f&#xf6;r st&#xf6;d i olika former till MR-f&#xf6;rsvarare och offer f&#xf6;r MR-&#xf6;vertr&#xe4;delser; f&#xf6;r monitorering och rapportering av MR-&#xf6;vertr&#xe4;delser; f&#xf6;r st&#xf6;d till och kapacitetsutveckling av r&#xe4;ttighetsb&#xe4;rare och organisationer. S&#xe4;rskilt fokus p&#xe5; kvinnor och ungdomar.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support through Tr&#xf3;caire to a human rights consortium f&#xf6;r support in different forms to human rights defenders and victims of human rights abuse; for monitoring and reporting of human rights abuse; for support to and capacity building of rights holders and organisations. Special focus on women and youth.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tr&#xf3;caire is working together with a Consortium of local civil society partners. The project has three intermediary outcomes:
1. Duty bearers are challenged by organised citizens to respect and protect human rights.
2. Reduced barriers to gender equality in civil and political rights. 
3. Equipped civil society organisations sustain their role of supporting citizens
and communities to exercise their rights.</narrative>
  </description>
